-- US-3134: colorways read from PRODUCT TITLES, for 24 brands.
--
-- 00756 could not read 101 held brands and said so: their Color variant option
-- is empty across enormous catalogues -- Everlane over 8,879 products, Boden
-- over 10,000. They are not colourless. They model each colourway as its own
-- PRODUCT, so the colour sits in the title and the harvester, which read only
-- the Color option, saw nothing.
--
-- scripts/ops/shopify-brand-harvest.mjs now reads titles too, and reports which
-- of the two it used. These rows are the title-derived half.
--
-- -- WHY THESE ROWS CARRY 0.55 AND NOT 0.75 -------------------------------
--
-- A variant option is a DECLARATION: the brand says "this product comes in
-- Slate Blue". A title suffix is a HEURISTIC: this tool decided that whatever
-- follows the last " | " is a colour. Both can be right and only one is stated,
-- so they must not be priced the same. Every row here is 0.55;
-- option-derived rows stay at 0.75.
--
-- -- FOUR TESTS, BECAUSE THE OBVIOUS ONE IS NOT ENOUGH -----------------------
--
-- Splitting every title on a separator produces confident garbage. The parser
-- decides PER BRAND whether a separator is really the colour position:
--
--   coverage    the separator must appear in at least half the titles, so it is
--               the brand's convention and not an accident in a few products
--   cardinality at least 8 distinct tails, so the tail VARIES like a colour
--               rather than being a repeated marketing suffix
--   shape       no size words, no style numbers, trailing parentheticals
--               stripped -- Allbirds writes "Natural Black (Dark Grey Sole)"
--   length      at most three words
--
-- The length rule exists because of Wax London, whose titles split into "Black
-- Organic Cotton Twill Shorts" -- an entire product description sitting exactly
-- where a colour would be. It cleared coverage and cardinality with room to
-- spare. Parkhurst was the same shape ("Saddle Waxy Commander"). Both are now
-- correctly read as having no title colour at all.
--
-- -- AND A FIFTH TEST, HERE RATHER THAN IN THE HARVESTER ---------------------
--
-- Ciele passes all four and is still wrong: its tails are PRODUCT LINES --
-- Athletics, Circle C, Century, Iconic Bar, Ninety SL. Short, varied,
-- consistent, and not colours.
--
-- So a brand must also have at least 15% of its tails resolve to a colour
-- family through aspect-normalize. A real colour position is full of Black,
-- Navy and Deep Navy; a product-line position resolves at nearly zero. This
-- check lives in the migration rather than the harvester because it needs the
-- colour table, and the harvester deliberately knows nothing about eBay.
--
-- ⚠ THIS IS THE WEAKEST RULE IN THE SET AND THE BAR IS CALIBRATED ON TWO
-- EXAMPLES. Ciele resolves at 0%. Warp + Weft resolves at 23% and is GENUINE --
-- JET BLACK, GARNET, INDUSTRIAL GREY, AMERICANO are its real denim wash names,
-- which is exactly the house-name vocabulary this KB exists to capture. A bar
-- at 30% dropped it; the bar is therefore 15%, which separates the one true
-- negative from the one true positive and nothing more. A product-line brand
-- that happened to resolve at 20% would pass. Widen the evidence before
-- trusting this number.
--
-- Rejected by it: ciele (44 tails, 0% resolve).
-- Rejected for too few tails: none.
--
-- -- SEEDED ------------------------------------------------------------------
--
-- 5756 colorways across 24 brands:
--     allbirds               90 colours  ' - ' at 97% coverage, 76% resolve
--     americangiant         387 colours  ' - ' at 97% coverage, 57% resolve
--     badbirdie             116 colours  ' - ' at 82% coverage, 46% resolve
--     birddogs              102 colours  ' - ' at 80% coverage, 81% resolve
--     brixton               399 colours  ' - ' at 94% coverage, 89% resolve
--     colorfulstandard       65 colours  ' - ' at 98% coverage, 83% resolve
--     criquet               120 colours  ' - ' at 98% coverage, 62% resolve
--     duer                  115 colours  ' - ' at 98% coverage, 61% resolve
--     everlane              379 colours  ' | ' at 93% coverage, 68% resolve
--     fairharbor            220 colours  ' | ' at 96% coverage, 62% resolve
--     folkclothing          400 colours  ' - ' at 80% coverage, 85% resolve
--     ironheart             200 colours  ' - ' at 88% coverage, 74% resolve
--     keen                  400 colours  ' | ' at 98% coverage, 71% resolve
--     kith                  398 colours  ' - ' at 82% coverage, 55% resolve
--     komodo                161 colours  ' - ' at 67% coverage, 78% resolve
--     kuiu                  196 colours  ' | ' at 99% coverage, 55% resolve
--     meshki                271 colours  ' - ' at 98% coverage, 85% resolve
--     passengerclothing     219 colours  ' - ' at 96% coverage, 81% resolve
--     percival              109 colours  ' | ' at 98% coverage, 87% resolve
--     polarskate            175 colours  ' - ' at 90% coverage, 87% resolve
--     rails                 400 colours  ' - ' at 98% coverage, 58% resolve
--     ryderwear             288 colours  ' - ' at 99% coverage, 77% resolve
--     thursdayboots         389 colours  ' | ' at 97% coverage, 56% resolve
--     warpweft              157 colours  ' | ' at 99% coverage, 23% resolve

